The '''Mustafar system''' was a [[Star system|solar system]] in the [[Atravis sector]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> that contained the [[Volcano|volcanic]] [[planet]] of [[Mustafar]],<ref name="Episode III" /> the [[gas giant]] [[Jestefad]]<ref name="Complete Locations" /> and its [[ocean]]ic [[moon]] [[Nur]],<ref name="Devoted" /> and another gas giant called [[Lefrani]],<ref name="Complete Locations" /> all of which [[orbit]]ed the [[star]] [[Priate]].<ref name="BMF17" />

==History==
{{Quote|I am sending you to the Mustafar system in the Outer Rim.|[[General]] [[Grievous]], to the Executive Separatist Council|<ref name="Episode III" />}}
During the [[Clone Wars]], the Mustafar system was affiliated with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. Mustafar was the final place for refuge for the [[Executive Separatist Council]], who were [[Mission to Mustafar|butchered]] by the newly-anointed [[Sith apprentice]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], whom they had been tricked into trusting by his [[Sith Master]] and their supposed ally, [[Darth Sidious]]. Afterward, Vader and his former mentor, [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], engaged in a fateful [[Duel on Mustafar]] that left Vader horribly injured, forcing the [[Sith Lord]] to live within a [[Darth Vader's armor|cybernetic suit]].<ref name="Episode III" />

[[File:CandiceDailey-DarkAspirations.png|thumb|left|250px|Darth Vader, dark lord of the Mustafar system]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], Vader requested control over Mustafar<ref name="Dark Lord 20">[[Darth Vader (2017) 20|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 20]]</ref> and built [[Fortress Vader]] in its [[Gahenn Plains]].<ref name="Dark Lord 23">[[Darth Vader (2017) 23|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 23]]</ref> The entire system fell under Vader's personal control.<ref name="Kenobi IV" /> Hoping to keep a close [[eye]] on his agents, he chose nearby Nur to be the [[Fortress Inquisitorius|base of operations]] for the [[Inquisitorius]], a group of [[Jedi hunter]]s under his command.<ref name="Inside Intel Inquisitorius">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-inside-intel-the-inquisitorius|text=''Star Wars'' Inside Intel: The Inquisitorius|int=Star Wars Inside Intel}}</ref> Vader's control over the Mustafar system was known to the [[Hidden Path]], an underground network dedicated to helping [[Force-sensitive]]s.<ref name="Kenobi IV" /> During the [[war against the Sith]], the [[Knights of Ren]] [[Heist on Vader's Castle|broke into]] Fortress Vader, which helped prove to Sidious they faced a determined enemy in what ended up being [[Crimson Dawn]].<ref name="Crimson Reign 5">[[Crimson Reign 5|''Crimson Reign'' 5]]</ref>

In the wake of Vader's death and redemption back into the [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] during the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Fortress Vader was abandoned. Vader's trapped former servant, [[Vaneé]], remained within, however. After being released,<ref name="Shadow of Darth Vader's Castle">''[[Star Wars Adventures: Shadow of Vader's Castle]]''</ref> Vaneé conducted a failed ritual he hoped would resurrect Vader. Skywalker's [[Force spirit]] ventured to Mustafar and his former castle to help guide Vaneé's captives out of the building.<ref name="Ghosts of Vader's Castle 5">[[Star Wars Adventures: Ghosts of Vader's Castle 5|''Star Wars Adventures: Ghosts of Vader's Castle'' 5]]</ref>

